<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhang Er</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 202 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhang Er was a statesman from the former state of Wei who joined the revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> and helped restore the kingdom of Zhao. In 206 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> made him King of Changshan, but his former friend <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-yu">Chen Yu</a> drove him out with help from Qi, and he joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-xin">Han Xin</a> conquered Zhao, Zhang Er was made King of Zhao in 203 BCE and died the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhang-er.jpg" alt="Zhang Er" width="320" height="539" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cjl2211 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zhang_er_poet_China_Blue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
